@prefix : <http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix c2sim: <http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/C2SIM#> .
@prefix smx: <http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/smx#> .
@prefix lox: <http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/lox#> .
@base <http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#> .

<http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx/plan> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx/plan/0.0.3> ;
    owl:imports <http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/lox> ;
    rdfs:comment """DRAFT — ASX Plan-Semantics module. Work in progress; not adopted by the ASX subgroup.

Extends the LOX plan constructs (PlanBody, PlanPhase, PlanPhaseTrigger) with the semantics required
to express autonomous-system behavior: failure outcomes and fallback branching (behavior-tree
Fallback/Selector), state-predicate guard conditions, composite and human-approval triggers,
repetition/persistence policies, goals with achievement conditions and commitment modes (BDI),
plan applicability conditions (plan pre-selection library), and intention/deviation reporting.
It also adds the failure-side dual of the LOX PlanPhaseCompletionCondition code list.
Design rationale and construct-by-construct derivation are in 'Plan-Semantics-Analysis.md'
in this directory.

v0.0.3 additions, from two validation inputs: (a) the three validation walks in
PlanSemanticsWalks/ (deviation vocabulary, repetition cadence, embarkation/endurance/mobility
predicates, late-bound product rule, action-taken reference, object-reference filter semantics);
(b) the standards-matrix verification pass in
../InstantiationReview/PlanSemantics-Walk.md against JAUS AS6062, STANAG 4586, MAVLink,
IEEE 1872.1-2024, FlexBE, and 4D/RCS (plan identity and supersession, suspension state,
task-disposition reporting, lost-link failsafe defaults with keep-in/keep-out predicate,
structured waypoints). Rules R15-R19 state the added execution semantics.

Additive REPORTING constructs (status and deviation report contents, new code individuals) degrade
gracefully for consumers that ignore unknown vocabulary. GATING and RESTRICTING constructs (triggers,
guards, timeouts, failure handling) are mandatory-to-understand: they narrow when and how a phase may
execute, so ignoring them removes the safety envelope. See rule R13.

NORMATIVE EXECUTION-SEMANTICS RULES. OWL cannot express execution semantics; the following rules are
normative for implementations of this module and are referenced from entity comments as R1..R19.
 R1  (outcomes) A plan phase reaches exactly one terminal outcome: PhaseSucceeded, PhaseFailed,
     PhaseAborted, or PhaseSkipped. PhasePending, PhaseInProgress, and PhaseSuspended are
     non-terminal states.
 R2  (sequencing) A lox:PriorPhaseCompletionTrigger fires only when the referenced phase's outcome
     is PhaseSucceeded or PhaseSkipped. Failure does not fire it; failed chains resolve via
     fallback (R7) or parent failure aggregation (R3), never by silently continuing.
 R3  (failure aggregation) hasPhaseFailureCondition carries only the member-aggregation policy:
     AnyTaskFailed (the default when omitted) or AllTasksFailed. "Task" includes subphases.
     When the policy is met, the phase fails immediately.
 R4  (implicit failure modes) Declaring hasPhaseTimeout or hasGuardCondition makes the corresponding
     failure mode live regardless of the aggregation policy: timeout expiry or guard violation fails
     the phase at once while it is in progress (guards are not evaluated during suspension; see R17).
     TimeoutExceeded and GuardViolated are used as failure-cause values in reports
     (hasPhaseFailureCauseCode), not as selectable aggregation policies.
 R5  (propagation on termination) When a phase reaches a terminal outcome, its in-flight member tasks
     are aborted (TASKABRT), in-flight or suspended subphases become PhaseAborted (a suspended
     member counts as in-flight for this rule), and not-yet-started members become PhaseSkipped.
 R6  (precedence) Completion and failure conditions are evaluated against event times, not report
     arrival times. If both are satisfiable for the same phase, failure takes precedence.
 R7  (fallback) When a phase fails and declares hasOnFailurePhaseReference, the referenced phase is
     activated. The referenced phase's mandatory trigger MUST be an OnPhaseFailureTrigger naming the
     failing phase; the two references must agree. If the fallback phase (or its own onward fallback
     chain) ultimately succeeds, the failed phase is treated as succeeded for purposes of its
     parent's completion and failure aggregation. Fallback chains MUST be acyclic, and a phase that
     has reached a terminal outcome may be re-entered only under an explicit repetition policy.
 R8  (fallback vs. policy) hasOnFailurePhaseReference provides peer-level fallback;
     the PriorityFallback execution policy provides alternative subphases. When both apply, a failed
     subphase's own fallback chain resolves before the parent advances to its next-priority
     alternative.
 R9  (composite AND) A CompositeTrigger with operator AllSubTriggers fires at the first instant at
     which every discrete sub-trigger (event, order, approval, prior-phase, phase-failure) has
     occurred AND every StateConditionTrigger sub-condition currently holds. Discrete sub-triggers
     latch once occurred; state conditions do not latch and must hold at the instant of firing.
 R10 (one-shot triggers) Phase triggers gate initial activation only and do not re-arm. Iterations
     of a repeated phase are governed solely by the repetition policy. PhaseFailed is reported as
     the terminal outcome only after the repetition policy is exhausted; per-attempt state is
     conveyed via hasAttemptNumber on PlanExecutionStatusContent.
 R11 (state evaluation) A StateConditionTrigger is level-triggered: it fires as soon as its
     condition evaluates true against the executing system's own world model, at or after the time
     the phase becomes eligible (including immediately, if already true). Different systems may
     legitimately hold different world models; the commander must treat such triggers as evaluated
     from the tasked system's perspective.
 R12 (condition conjunction) Repeated values of hasGuardCondition, hasAchievementCondition,
     hasGoalFailureCondition, and hasContextCondition are conjunctive. Disjunction and richer
     composition are provided only at the trigger level (CompositeTrigger) in this version.
 R13 (fail-closed interoperability) A consumer that cannot interpret a phase's trigger — including
     the trigger subclasses defined here — MUST treat the phase as not triggerable, MUST NOT execute
     it, and SHOULD report the inability (ACKNOTUNDSTD). Plans using this module's gating constructs
     SHOULD only be transmitted to consumers that have negotiated the module at initialization.
 R14 (plan library) AutonomousPlanBody instances carrying hasContextCondition MUST be transmitted
     with isToBeExecutedNow = false and only to consumers that have negotiated this module. Context
     conditions are re-evaluated during execution: when the active plan's context becomes false and
     another transmitted plan for the same Goal is applicable, the executing system switches and
     reports a PlanSwitched deviation.
 R15 (late-bound products) A phase product that will not exist until runtime is referenced by a
     pre-allocated UUID: the tasking side allocates the UUID (in hasPhaseProductReference and in any
     consuming condition or task references), and the producing system binds that UUID to the actual
     object when it publishes it. Consumers treat an unbound product reference as not-yet-available,
     never as an error, until the producing phase reports a terminal outcome.
 R16 (plan identity and supersession) Every AutonomousPlanBody carries a hasPlanID, distinct from
     message identity. A plan whose hasSupersededPlanReference names a previously received plan
     replaces it: the superseded plan MUST NOT be started thereafter, and if it is executing, the
     receiving system treats the supersession as SuspendPlanExecution on it before starting the
     superseding plan under its own triggers and isToBeExecutedNow. A superseded plan MUST NOT be
     resumed; when the superseding plan first activates a phase, the superseded plan's suspended
     phases become PhaseAborted (with the R5 disposition applied to their members) - until then the
     superseded plan remains suspended so that abort and status verbs can still address it.
     Supersession chains MUST be acyclic. A system that does not hold the referenced plan SHOULD
     report the gap and request retransmission rather than execute the amendment blind.
 R17 (suspension) On SuspendPlanExecution, in-flight phases move to PhaseSuspended (non-terminal,
     R1). While a plan is suspended no phase of it may be activated; phase timeouts and
     repetition-interval timers pause; guard conditions are not evaluated. Discrete trigger events
     occurring during suspension latch and are honored at resume; state conditions and
     completion/failure conditions are evaluated afresh at resume, like guards. On
     ResumePlanExecution, guards are re-evaluated first and top-down - a guard that does not hold
     fails the phase at resume (R4), and a phase that fails at resume terminates per R5 before its
     descendants' guards are evaluated - then timeout clocks continue from their paused values.
     AbortPlanExecution from suspension yields PhaseAborted.
 R18 (lost-link precedence) When communications with the command node have been lost for longer
     than hasLostLinkTimeout, the executing system (1) switches to an applicable transmitted plan
     whose context conditions hold (R14), if one exists; otherwise (2) executes the plan's declared
     hasLostLinkBehaviorCode; otherwise (3) reverts to its platform-default failsafe. Step (1) IS
     the R14 switching machinery, with communications loss as the driving context change over the
     plans already transmitted and held on the platform: if a CommsDenied-gated variant becomes
     applicable under R14 before hasLostLinkTimeout elapses (a shorter threshold duration), R14
     governs and the switch occurs then. A switch or behavior made while the link is down is
     reported on restoration as a single LostLinkBehaviorActivated deviation naming what ran (a
     separate PlanSwitched deviation is not sent for the same transition). On restoration of
     communications the system reports the deviation covering the interval.
 R19 (waypoint traversal) The waypoints of a StructuredRoute are visited in ascending
     hasWaypointSequenceNumber, which MUST be unique within the route; ordering is normative from
     the sequence numbers, never from serialization order. On arrival at a waypoint the system
     first executes the referenced waypoint task (if any) to a terminal status, then loiters for
     hasLoiterDuration (if given), then proceeds. If the waypoint task ends TASKFAILD, the failure
     propagates per R3 to the phase executing the movement (traversal does not silently continue);
     the system proceeds past the waypoint only on task completion, or when no task is referenced.
     hasTransitSpeed applies to the leg arriving at the waypoint. A hasWaypointArrivalTime is an
     authoring commitment - the author must reconcile it with upstream waypoint tasks and loiter
     durations; a projected or actual miss is reported (hasEstimatedPhaseCompletionTime or a
     deviation report) and does not of itself fail the movement task.""" ;
    owl:versionInfo "C2SIM ASX Plan-Semantics module v0.0.3 DRAFT" .

#################################################################
#    External entities referenced (declaration stubs)
#################################################################

c2sim:C2SIMContent rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:Code rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:DesiredEffectCode rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:Duration rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:Location rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:ReportContent rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:TaskActionCode rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:TaskStatus rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:TaskStatusCode rdf:type owl:Class .
c2sim:TimeInstant rdf:type owl:Class .
lox:PlanBody rdf:type owl:Class .
lox:PlanPhase rdf:type owl:Class .
lox:PlanPhaseTrigger rdf:type owl:Class .
smx:Route rdf:type owl:Class .

c2sim:UUIDBase rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .

c2sim:hasCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
c2sim:hasDesiredEffectCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
c2sim:hasDuration rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
c2sim:hasLocation rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .
c2sim:hasTimeInstant rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .

c2sim:hasActorReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .
c2sim:hasEventReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .
c2sim:hasReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .
c2sim:hasUUID rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .
lox:hasPlanPhaseReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .
lox:hasTriggerPhase rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .
smx:hasConfidenceLevel rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty .

#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasCondition
:hasCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "Containment of an inline Condition structure. Specialized subproperties identify the role the condition plays." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasGuardCondition
:hasGuardCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasCondition ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "An invariant that must hold for the duration of a plan phase. Violation while the phase is active fails the phase immediately (rule R4). Repeated guards are conjunctive (R12)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasContextCondition
:hasContextCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasCondition ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "An applicability condition on a plan: the plan may be selected for execution only while this condition holds, and it is re-evaluated during execution (rule R14). When several plans reference the same Goal, context conditions determine which is applicable (BDI-style context condition; HTN method precondition)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasAchievementCondition
:hasAchievementCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasCondition ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "The end state that defines achievement of a Goal. The Goal is achieved when this condition becomes true. Repeated values are conjunctive (R12)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasGoalFailureCondition
:hasGoalFailureCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasCondition ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "A condition under which a Goal is to be considered unachievable and abandoned." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasDeviationCondition
:hasDeviationCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasCondition ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "The world-state condition that caused a reported deviation, when the cause was a Condition rather than a discrete Event. Where the condition instance carried a UUID, the report may cite it by reference instead." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRepetitionUntilCondition
:hasRepetitionUntilCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasCondition ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "The loop-termination condition of a phase whose repetition policy is RepeatUntilCondition. The inherited LOX completion condition closes each iteration; this condition closes the loop (e.g. repeat detect-and-neutralize passes until the route-clear condition holds)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasInfeasibilityCondition
:hasInfeasibilityCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasCondition ;
    rdfs:range :Condition ;
    rdfs:comment "In a TaskDispositionReportContent whose status is TASKRJCT, the world-state condition that makes the task infeasible for the tasked system - the machine-readable form of the 4D/RCS 'cannot do because of condition xyz' reply. Optional; rationale text carries the human-readable form." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasGoal
:hasGoal rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range :Goal ;
    rdfs:comment "Containment of an inline Goal definition. Goals are defined inline once (typically in the AutonomousPlanBody that first pursues them) and referenced elsewhere by UUID via hasGoalReference." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasSubTrigger
:hasSubTrigger rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range lox:PlanPhaseTrigger ;
    rdfs:comment "A constituent trigger of a CompositeTrigger. Sub-triggers may themselves be composite, permitting nested logical structure." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasLogicalOperatorCode
:hasLogicalOperatorCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :LogicalOperatorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The logical operator combining the sub-triggers of a CompositeTrigger. See rule R9 for the semantics of AllSubTriggers over mixed discrete and state sub-triggers." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasConditionPredicateCode
:hasConditionPredicateCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The predicate that a Condition evaluates. Each predicate code documents which of the typed condition properties (subject reference, object reference, threshold value, threshold duration) it uses and how." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasPhaseFailureCondition
:hasPhaseFailureCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :PhaseFailureCondition ;
    rdfs:comment "The member-aggregation failure policy of a plan phase: AnyTaskFailed (default when omitted) or AllTasksFailed, where members are the phase's tasks and subphases (rule R3). Timeout and guard failures are implicit whenever hasPhaseTimeout or hasGuardCondition are declared (rule R4) and are not selected here. The failure-side dual of lox:hasPlanPhaseCompletionCondition." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasPhaseFailureCauseCode
:hasPhaseFailureCauseCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :PhaseFailureCondition ;
    rdfs:comment "In a report, the cause of a phase failure: the aggregation policy that was met (AnyTaskFailed, AllTasksFailed) or an implicit failure mode (TimeoutExceeded, GuardViolated)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasExecutionPolicyCode
:hasExecutionPolicyCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :PhaseExecutionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The policy governing execution of the subphases of a plan phase. Subphases of a policy-bearing parent carry a ParentPhasePolicyTrigger in their mandatory trigger slot; ordering under SequentialInOrder and PriorityFallback is given by hasPhasePriority. If subphases instead carry their own triggers, those triggers must be consistent with the policy; on conflict the policy is normative." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRepetitionPolicyCode
:hasRepetitionPolicyCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :RepetitionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The repetition/persistence policy of a plan phase: execute once, retry on failure, repeat until a condition holds, or maintain continuously as a standing behavior. See rule R10: the phase trigger gates only initial activation; iterations are governed by this policy." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasPhaseOutcomeCode
:hasPhaseOutcomeCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The execution state or terminal outcome of a plan phase, as reported in a PlanExecutionStatusContent." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasGoalCommitmentCode
:hasGoalCommitmentCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :GoalCommitmentCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The commitment mode of a Goal: achieve once, maintain continuously, or achieve then maintain. This qualifies the goal's success-condition temporality; the executing agent's reconsideration strategy is deliberately not modeled." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasDeviationTypeCode
:hasDeviationTypeCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The category of autonomous deviation being reported in a PlanDeviationReportContent." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRequiredAutonomyLevelCode
:hasRequiredAutonomyLevelCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :AutonomyLevelCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The level of autonomy at which a plan phase is to be executed. Permits graded, phase-dependent autonomy within a single plan (e.g. autonomous transit, supervised engagement)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasPhaseTimeout
:hasPhaseTimeout rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasDuration ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:Duration ;
    rdfs:comment "Maximum duration for a plan phase, measured from phase start. Declaring it makes the TimeoutExceeded failure mode live (rule R4)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasApprovalTimeout
:hasApprovalTimeout rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasDuration ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:Duration ;
    rdfs:comment "Maximum duration a HumanApprovalTrigger waits for approval before the timeout disposition applies." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasThresholdDuration
:hasThresholdDuration rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasDuration ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:Duration ;
    rdfs:comment "A duration parameter of a Condition, where its predicate calls for one (e.g. CommsDenied for longer than this duration; TimeElapsedSince a referenced event)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasEstimatedPhaseCompletionTime
:hasEstimatedPhaseCompletionTime rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasTimeInstant ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:TimeInstant ;
    rdfs:comment "The executing system's current estimate of when the reported plan phase will complete." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRepetitionInterval
:hasRepetitionInterval rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasDuration ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:Duration ;
    rdfs:comment "Cadence between iterations of a phase under a RepeatUntilCondition or MaintainContinuously repetition policy: the interval from the start of one iteration to the start of the next (revisit rate for persistent-watch and periodic-survey behaviors; MDARS revisit cadence, cooperative-MCM repeat-on-cadence search). Paused while the phase is suspended (rule R17). If an iteration overruns the interval, the next begins immediately on completion." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasLostLinkTimeout
:hasLostLinkTimeout rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasDuration ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:Duration ;
    rdfs:comment "Duration of continuous communications loss with the command node after which the lost-link disposition of rule R18 applies. STANAG 4586 lost-link and MAVLink failsafe analog." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasLoiterDuration
:hasLoiterDuration rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasDuration ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:Duration ;
    rdfs:comment "Time to hold at a RouteWaypoint after any waypoint task completes and before proceeding to the next waypoint (rule R19). STANAG 4586 loiter-duration analog; loiter pattern selection is left to the platform." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasWaypointArrivalTime
:hasWaypointArrivalTime rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasTimeInstant ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:TimeInstant ;
    rdfs:comment "Required arrival time at a RouteWaypoint (time-on-target scheduling; STANAG 4586 arrival-time analog). How the platform paces itself to meet it is not modeled." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasLostLinkBehaviorCode
:hasLostLinkBehaviorCode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasCode ;
    rdfs:range :FailsafeBehaviorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The failsafe behavior a plan declares for loss of communications with the command node (rule R18: an applicable transmitted contingency plan takes precedence; this code is the declared floor above the platform default). Mandatory-to-understand in effect: a consumer that cannot interpret it retains only its platform default - commanders should confirm module negotiation before relying on it (R13)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRouteWaypoint
:hasRouteWaypoint rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range :RouteWaypoint ;
    rdfs:comment "Containment of the ordered waypoints of a StructuredRoute. Ordering is carried by each waypoint's hasWaypointSequenceNumber (rule R19), never by serialization order." .

#################################################################
#    Data properties
#################################################################

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasOnFailurePhaseReference
:hasOnFailurePhaseReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf lox:hasPlanPhaseReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the plan phase to be activated if this phase fails (behavior-tree Fallback/Selector semantics; activation semantics for JC3IEDM ALT/HASPRV task relations). The referenced phase's mandatory trigger MUST be an OnPhaseFailureTrigger naming this phase, and the two references must agree (rule R7). Further alternatives are expressed by chaining: the fallback phase may itself declare a fallback. Chains must be acyclic. Interaction with the PriorityFallback execution policy is defined by rule R8." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasOnTimeoutPhaseReference
:hasOnTimeoutPhaseReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf lox:hasPlanPhaseReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the plan phase to be activated if a HumanApprovalTrigger times out without approval, or is refused (e.g. a safe-hold or withdraw phase). If omitted, the gated phase becomes PhaseSkipped; per rule R2 a skipped phase satisfies downstream PriorPhaseCompletionTriggers, so the remainder of the plan proceeds." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasGoalReference
:hasGoalReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the Goal that a plan, plan phase, or task is intended to achieve. The referenced Goal must have been defined inline (hasGoal) in a previously transmitted or accompanying message." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasActiveGoalReference
:hasActiveGoalReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :hasGoalReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the Goal the reporting system is currently committed to (its active intention)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasApprovingEntity
:hasApprovingEntity rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasActorReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the ActorEntity whose approval satisfies a HumanApprovalTrigger. Approval is conveyed by a message from this entity with CommunicativeActTypeCode Agree or Confirm whose body references the gated plan phase's UUID; refusal by a Refuse message. The precise message-body binding is an open item for message-schema definition." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasTriggeringEventReference
:hasTriggeringEventReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasEventReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the Event that caused a reported deviation, when the cause was a discrete Event." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasConditionSubjectReference
:hasConditionSubjectReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the entity, task, location, route, or area that a Condition's predicate is evaluated against (the predicate's subject)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasConditionObjectReference
:hasConditionObjectReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to the second participant of a binary Condition predicate (e.g. the location for EntityAtLocation; the reference entity for EntityWithinRange; the counterpart node for CommsAvailable; the anchor event for TimeElapsedSince). Where a predicate's documentation says the object reference is a FILTER (e.g. ThreatDetectedInArea), it names an entity-type definition rather than an entity instance - in base C2SIM terms a c2sim:NamedEntityType or c2sim:SISOEntityType structure carrying a UUID; the referenceable form of the type filter is an open item for message-schema definition, tied to review item X4 - and the predicate is restricted to detections matching that type; absent the filter, any qualifying detection satisfies the predicate." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasThresholdValue
:hasThresholdValue rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:double ;
    rdfs:comment "A numeric parameter of a Condition, where its predicate calls for one. Units are defined by the predicate code (e.g. meters for EntityWithinRange and EntityAtLocation tolerance; a 0..1 fraction for AreaCoverageAchieved and EstimateConfidenceAbove; a health fraction for EntityHealthBelow)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#isNegated
:isNegated rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:comment "When true, the Condition's truth value is the negation of its predicate (default false). Provides guard polarity and else-branches without a general expression language (e.g. guard 'no hazard on route' = HazardOnRoute with isNegated true)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRepetitionLimit
:hasRepetitionLimit rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rdfs:comment "Upper bound on the number of executions of a phase under a RetryOnFailure or RepeatUntilCondition repetition policy." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasAttemptNumber
:hasAttemptNumber rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rdfs:comment "In a PlanExecutionStatusContent, the current attempt number of a phase executing under a repetition policy (rule R10: PhaseFailed is terminal only after the policy is exhausted)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasPhasePriority
:hasPhasePriority rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rdfs:comment "Ordering rank of a subphase under a parent phase whose execution policy is SequentialInOrder or PriorityFallback; lower values run/are attempted first. RDF property values are unordered, so ordering is always explicit via this property, never by declaration order." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasGoalPriority
:hasGoalPriority rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rdfs:comment "Relative priority of a Goal for deconfliction when an executing system holds multiple concurrent goals; lower values take precedence. This version does not define preemption semantics between running plans; priority informs the executing system's own deliberation." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasPhaseProductReference
:hasPhaseProductReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to a data product (e.g. a surveyed route, a hazard map, a track) that this phase publishes on completion for consumption by other entities' tasks — the interoperability-visible portion of a producer/consumer handoff, such as a scout advertising a safe route to a transport vehicle. Definition of product object types is left to the ASX message layer." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasPlanID
:hasPlanID rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "The identity of a plan, distinct from the identity of any message that carries it (rule R16). Follows the OrderBody hasOrderID idiom; JAUS AS6062 mission-ID and STANAG 4586 mission-number precedent. Enables supersession (hasSupersededPlanReference), status reporting against a plan, and holding several concurrent plans." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasSupersededPlanReference
:hasSupersededPlanReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "The hasPlanID of a previously transmitted plan that this plan replaces (rule R16). The plan-granularity activation semantics for the JC3IEDM IMO ('is a modification of') task relation; JAUS Remove/Replace Messages analog. Supports the mid-mission re-tasking pattern: suspend, transmit superseding plan, resume." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRallyPointReference
:hasRallyPointReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to a pre-designated safe location (a Location or MapGraphic defined at initialization or in the plan) for the ReturnToRallyPoint failsafe behavior. Repeatable; the system selects the reachable rally point per its own navigation state. MAVLink rally-point analog." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasActionTakenReference
:hasActionTakenReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "In a PlanDeviationReportContent, reference to the task or plan phase the system activated as a result of the deviation (e.g. the fallback phase, the replanned route task), or the task or phase within which the reported adjustment was made (for BehaviorAdjusted). Optional: where no referenceable object exists, the action taken rides in the rationale text." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasWaypointTaskReference
:hasWaypointTaskReference rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf c2sim:hasReference ;
    rdfs:range c2sim:UUIDBase ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to a previously defined Task to be executed on arrival at this waypoint (rule R19): the STANAG 4586 payload-action-waypoint and Nav2 waypoint-task-executor pattern (sensor point/collect, drop, pickup, report). The task's own performing entity must be the platform traversing the route." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasWaypointSequenceNumber
:hasWaypointSequenceNumber rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rdfs:comment "Ordering rank of a waypoint within a StructuredRoute; visited in ascending order, unique within the route (rule R19). Explicit because RDF property values are unordered - this replaces the fragile document-order convention of bare location lists." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasTransitSpeed
:hasTransitSpeed rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:double ;
    rdfs:comment "Commanded speed, in meters per second, for the route leg arriving at this waypoint (rule R19). STANAG 4586 waypoint-speed analog." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasConditionText
:hasConditionText rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Human-readable statement of a Condition, for operator display and as an escape hatch where the predicate vocabulary is insufficient. Systems must not rely on this text for automated evaluation." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#hasRationaleText
:hasRationaleText rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Human-understandable explanation of why the reporting system took the reported action or deviation." .

#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#Condition
:Condition rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:C2SIMContent ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasConditionPredicateCode ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :ConditionPredicateCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasConditionSubjectReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasConditionObjectReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasThresholdValue ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:double ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasThresholdDuration ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:Duration ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :isNegated ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:boolean ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty c2sim:hasUUID ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasConditionText ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:string ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A machine-evaluable predicate over world state: a predicate code, optional negation, an optional subject reference, and typed parameters (object reference, threshold value, threshold duration) whose use is defined per predicate. Conditions serve as phase guards, trigger conditions, loop-termination conditions, goal achievement/failure criteria, and plan applicability (context) conditions. A Condition may carry a UUID so reports can cite the specific condition that fired or was violated. Deliberately code-based rather than a general expression language; conjunction of repeated conditions is defined by rule R12 and disjunction is provided at the trigger level (CompositeTrigger)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#StateConditionTrigger
:StateConditionTrigger rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf lox:PlanPhaseTrigger ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasCondition ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A plan phase trigger that fires when a world-state Condition evaluates true (level-triggered, rule R11), in contrast to lox:EventTrigger which is anchored to the occurrence time of a discrete reported Event. This is the module's mechanism for runtime reactivity and the behavior-tree guard/condition-node primitive." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#CompositeTrigger
:CompositeTrigger rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf lox:PlanPhaseTrigger ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasSubTrigger ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass lox:PlanPhaseTrigger ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasLogicalOperatorCode ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :LogicalOperatorCode ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A plan phase trigger composed of two or more sub-triggers combined by a logical operator (AllSubTriggers: rule R9 — discrete sub-triggers latch, state conditions must currently hold; AnySubTrigger: fires when any sub-trigger fires). Nesting composite triggers yields and/or trees while respecting the exactly-one hasPlanPhaseTrigger cardinality of lox:PlanPhase. Negation is provided on Condition (isNegated), not as an operator. k-of-n voting (e.g. any 2 of 3 sensors confirm) is a candidate future operator." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#HumanApprovalTrigger
:HumanApprovalTrigger rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf lox:PlanPhaseTrigger ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasApprovingEntity ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasApprovalTimeout ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:Duration ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasOnTimeoutPhaseReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A plan phase trigger satisfied only by explicit approval from the referenced authority (Agree/Confirm message referencing the gated phase). A Refuse message from that authority, or expiry of hasApprovalTimeout, immediately applies the timeout disposition: activate hasOnTimeoutPhaseReference if given, else the gated phase becomes PhaseSkipped. Provides on-the-loop gating of designated phases (notably engagement or other lethal-effect phases), making engagement authority an inspectable property of the plan and linking level of autonomy to human approval requirements. Typically composed with tactical triggers via CompositeTrigger. NOTE rule R13: this is a mandatory-to-understand construct — consumers that cannot interpret it must fail closed (never execute the gated phase)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#OnPhaseFailureTrigger
:OnPhaseFailureTrigger rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf lox:PlanPhaseTrigger ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty lox:hasTriggerPhase ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A plan phase trigger that fires when the referenced phase reaches the PhaseFailed outcome — the failure-side dual of lox:PriorPhaseCompletionTrigger. This is the sanctioned trigger for phases referenced by hasOnFailurePhaseReference (rule R7), satisfying the LOX exactly-one-trigger requirement while guaranteeing the fallback phase cannot activate independently of the failure path." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#ParentPhasePolicyTrigger
:ParentPhasePolicyTrigger rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf lox:PlanPhaseTrigger ;
    rdfs:comment "A plan phase trigger whose firing is controlled entirely by the parent phase's execution policy (hasExecutionPolicyCode): the parent activates the subphase when the policy dictates (in hasPhasePriority order under SequentialInOrder/PriorityFallback, immediately under ParallelAll/ParallelAny). Fills the mandatory trigger slot of policy-managed subphases without introducing an independent activation path." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#AutonomousPlanPhase
:AutonomousPlanPhase rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf lox:PlanPhase ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasPhaseFailureCondition ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :PhaseFailureCondition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasOnFailurePhaseReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasExecutionPolicyCode ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :PhaseExecutionPolicyCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRepetitionPolicyCode ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :RepetitionPolicyCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRepetitionUntilCondition ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRepetitionLimit ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRepetitionInterval ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:Duration ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasGuardCondition ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasPhaseTimeout ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:Duration ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRequiredAutonomyLevelCode ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :AutonomyLevelCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasPhasePriority ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasPhaseProductReference ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasGoalReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A lox:PlanPhase enriched with autonomous-execution semantics, all optional: a failure aggregation policy and fallback phase reference (rules R3, R7, R8), guard conditions (R4, R12), an execution policy over subphases, a repetition/persistence policy with loop-termination condition, attempt limit, and iteration cadence (R10, R17), a timeout (R4), a required level of autonomy, a priority rank under ordered policies, published data products (late-bound per R15), and a reference to the Goal the phase serves. Reporting additions degrade gracefully; gating additions are mandatory-to-understand (R13)." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#AutonomousPlanBody
:AutonomousPlanBody rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf lox:PlanBody ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasPlanID ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasSupersededPlanReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasGoal ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Goal ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasGoalReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasContextCondition ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasLostLinkBehaviorCode ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :FailsafeBehaviorCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasLostLinkTimeout ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:Duration ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRallyPointReference ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A lox:PlanBody with plan identity (hasPlanID, exactly one - rule R16), optional supersession of a prior plan (hasSupersededPlanReference, R16), inline Goal definitions (hasGoal), the Goal it is intended to achieve (hasGoalReference), applicability context conditions, and a declared lost-link disposition (hasLostLinkBehaviorCode / hasLostLinkTimeout / hasRallyPointReference - rule R18). Several AutonomousPlanBody instances referencing the same Goal with different context conditions constitute a transmitted plan pre-selection library (primary, degraded-comms, contested variants); per rule R14 such variants MUST carry isToBeExecutedNow = false, MUST only be sent to consumers that have negotiated this module, and plan switches are reported via PlanSwitched. Runtime subgoaling and agent reconsideration strategies are deliberately not modeled." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#Goal
:Goal rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:C2SIMContent ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasAchievementCondition ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasGoalFailureCondition ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasGoalCommitmentCode ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :GoalCommitmentCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty c2sim:hasDesiredEffectCode ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:DesiredEffectCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasGoalPriority ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty c2sim:hasUUID ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A desired end state, distinct from any procedure for achieving it: achievement condition(s) (conjunctive, R12), optional failure/abandonment conditions, a commitment mode (achieve once / maintain / achieve then maintain), optional links to the existing DesiredEffectCode vocabulary, and a priority for deconfliction. Goals are defined inline via hasGoal on an AutonomousPlanBody and referenced elsewhere by UUID. Enables goal-directed tasking (an AchieveGoal task conveying end state, constraints, and ROE) as well as goal-annotated procedural plans. Maintenance goals provide standing/persistent tasking semantics." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#PlanExecutionStatusContent
:PlanExecutionStatusContent rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:ReportContent ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty lox:hasPlanPhaseReference ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasPhaseOutcomeCode ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :PhaseOutcomeCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasPhaseFailureCauseCode ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :PhaseFailureCondition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasAttemptNumber ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasActiveGoalReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasEstimatedPhaseCompletionTime ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:TimeInstant ] ;
    rdfs:comment "Report content conveying plan-execution state at phase granularity: the referenced phase, its status/outcome, the failure cause where applicable, the current attempt number under a repetition policy, the goal currently being pursued (the reporting system's active intention), and estimated completion time. Complements the task-level TaskStatus report content. An additive reporting construct: degrades gracefully for consumers that ignore it." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#PlanDeviationReportContent
:PlanDeviationReportContent rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:ReportContent ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasDeviationTypeCode ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :DeviationTypeCode ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasTriggeringEventReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasDeviationCondition ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty lox:hasPlanPhaseReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRationaleText ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasActionTakenReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty smx:hasConfidenceLevel ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:double ] ;
    rdfs:comment "Report content sent whenever the executing system exercises an autonomous choice not scripted by the operator: what kind of deviation occurred, what event or condition triggered it, the affected plan phase, a human-understandable rationale, optionally the task or phase activated in response (hasActionTakenReference), and the system's confidence. Follows the explainability schema (event, action, reasoning, operational change, confidence) identified in the ASX reference materials. An additive reporting construct: degrades gracefully." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#TaskDispositionReportContent
:TaskDispositionReportContent rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:TaskStatus ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRationaleText ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasInfeasibilityCondition ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :Condition ] ;
    rdfs:comment "A c2sim:TaskStatus specialized for the tasking handshake: the inherited hasCurrentTask targets the specific task and the inherited hasTaskStatusCode carries its disposition (TASKACPT accepted / TASKRJCT rejected, plus the lifecycle codes), optionally with a rationale and, for rejections, the machine-readable infeasibility condition. Closes the gap that acknowledgment codes (ACKFAIL/ACKSUCC etc.) are message-level and cannot target one task of a multi-task order. FIPA agree/refuse and the 4D/RCS 'cannot do because' reply, in C2SIM idiom. An additive reporting construct: degrades gracefully." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#AutonomyLevelCode
:AutonomyLevelCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Level of autonomy at which a system or plan phase operates. The existing ASX individuals Teleop, ReCont, Automated, and FullAuto are intended to be re-typed as members of this class; anchoring to an external scale (ALFUS / 4D-RCS) is a subgroup decision item." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#FailsafeBehaviorCode
:FailsafeBehaviorCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Declared default behavior for loss of communications with the command node (rule R18). STANAG 4586 lost-link procedure and MAVLink failsafe/RTL precedent." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#RouteWaypoint
:RouteWaypoint rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:C2SIMContent ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasWaypointSequenceNumber ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty c2sim:hasLocation ;
          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:Location ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasTransitSpeed ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange xsd:double ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasWaypointArrivalTime ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:TimeInstant ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasLoiterDuration ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass c2sim:Duration ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasWaypointTaskReference ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty c2sim:hasUUID ;
          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onDataRange c2sim:UUIDBase ] ;
    rdfs:comment "One waypoint of a StructuredRoute: an explicit sequence number (rule R19), a location, and optional per-point attributes - transit speed for the arriving leg, required arrival time, post-arrival loiter duration, and a task to execute on arrival. Brings SMX routes to the per-waypoint expressiveness of STANAG 4586 waypoint messages (#13002-#13004) and MAVLink mission items, which the base standard's bare location lists (ordered only by serialization) cannot carry." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#StructuredRoute
:StructuredRoute rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf smx:Route ,
        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty :hasRouteWaypoint ;
          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
          owl:onClass :RouteWaypoint ] ;
    rdfs:comment "An smx:Route whose points are RouteWaypoint objects with explicit ordering and per-point attributes (rule R19). Remains a valid smx:Route/MapGraphic for consumers that only understand the base representation; module-aware consumers use the waypoint structure. A movement task references it via hasMapGraphicID exactly as it would a plain Route." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#LogicalOperatorCode
:LogicalOperatorCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Logical operator combining the sub-triggers of a CompositeTrigger." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#ConditionPredicateCode
:ConditionPredicateCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "The predicate vocabulary for Condition. Each code defines the semantics of the subject/object references and the meaning and units of the threshold value/duration. The list is intentionally small and scenario-driven; extensions add individuals as requirements are evidenced." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#PhaseFailureCondition
:PhaseFailureCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Codes for phase failure: the selectable member-aggregation policies (AnyTaskFailed, AllTasksFailed — rule R3) and the implicit failure modes (TimeoutExceeded, GuardViolated — rule R4) used as failure-cause values in reports. Named without the -Code suffix to parallel its LOX completion-side dual, lox:PlanPhaseCompletionCondition." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#PhaseExecutionPolicyCode
:PhaseExecutionPolicyCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Policy governing how the subphases of a plan phase are executed. See hasExecutionPolicyCode for the interaction with subphase triggers." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#RepetitionPolicyCode
:RepetitionPolicyCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Policy governing repetition or persistence of a plan phase." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#PhaseOutcomeCode
:PhaseOutcomeCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Execution states (PhasePending, PhaseInProgress, PhaseSuspended) and terminal outcomes (PhaseSucceeded, PhaseFailed, PhaseAborted, PhaseSkipped) of a plan phase - see rules R1 and R17." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#GoalCommitmentCode
:GoalCommitmentCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Commitment mode of a Goal." .

###  http://www.sisostds.org/ontologies/asx#DeviationTypeCode
:DeviationTypeCode rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf c2sim:Code ;
    rdfs:comment "Category of an autonomous deviation reported in a PlanDeviationReportContent." .

#################################################################
#    Individuals
#################################################################

###  Logical operators

:AllSubTriggers rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :LogicalOperatorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The composite trigger fires when all sub-triggers are satisfied — discrete sub-triggers latch once occurred; state-condition sub-triggers must hold at the instant of firing (rule R9)." .

:AnySubTrigger rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :LogicalOperatorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The composite trigger fires when any sub-trigger fires." .

###  Phase failure conditions

:AnyTaskFailed rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseFailureCondition ;
    rdfs:comment "Aggregation policy (default): the phase fails when any of its member tasks or subphases fails." .

:AllTasksFailed rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseFailureCondition ;
    rdfs:comment "Aggregation policy: the phase fails only when all of its member tasks or subphases have failed." .

:TimeoutExceeded rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseFailureCondition ;
    rdfs:comment "Failure cause (implicit mode, rule R4): the phase's hasPhaseTimeout duration expired before its completion condition was met. Not selectable as an aggregation policy; live whenever hasPhaseTimeout is declared." .

:GuardViolated rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseFailureCondition ;
    rdfs:comment "Failure cause (implicit mode, rule R4): a guard condition of the phase ceased to hold while the phase was active. Not selectable as an aggregation policy; live whenever hasGuardCondition is declared." .

###  Phase outcomes

:PhasePending rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The phase has not yet been triggered." .

:PhaseInProgress rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The phase has been triggered and is executing." .

:PhaseSuspended rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Non-terminal state (rules R1, R17): execution paused by SuspendPlanExecution (or by supersession, R16), state retained. Timeouts and repetition intervals pause; guards are re-evaluated at resume. Exits to PhaseInProgress on ResumePlanExecution or PhaseAborted on AbortPlanExecution. JAUS Pause/Resume Mission analog." .

:PhaseSucceeded rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The phase met its completion condition (or its fallback chain ultimately succeeded, rule R7)." .

:PhaseFailed rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The phase met its failure condition, after any repetition policy was exhausted (rule R10) and any fallback chain also failed (rule R7). Distinct from PhaseAborted (stopped by command)." .

:PhaseAborted rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Execution of the phase was stopped by command, exception, or termination of its parent (rule R5) before completion or failure." .

:PhaseSkipped rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseOutcomeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The phase was never executed because control flow bypassed it (an unneeded fallback, an approval refusal/timeout with no timeout phase, or a sibling's failure under rule R5). A skipped phase satisfies downstream PriorPhaseCompletionTriggers (rule R2)." .

###  Phase execution policies

:SequentialInOrder rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseExecutionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Subphases execute one at a time in hasPhasePriority order. With the default AnyTaskFailed aggregation this yields behavior-tree Sequence semantics: a subphase failure fails the parent immediately and remaining subphases are skipped (rules R3, R5)." .

:ParallelAll rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseExecutionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Subphases activate concurrently; the parent completes when all complete. Corresponds to lox:AllTasksComplete at subphase granularity. On parent termination, in-flight subphases are aborted (rule R5)." .

:ParallelAny rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseExecutionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Subphases activate concurrently; the parent completes when any completes, and the remaining in-flight subphases are then aborted (rule R5). Corresponds to lox:OneTaskComplete at subphase granularity." .

:PriorityFallback rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PhaseExecutionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Subphases are attempted one at a time in hasPhasePriority order; the parent succeeds when one succeeds and fails when all have failed. Behavior-tree Fallback/Selector semantics as a containment policy; interaction with per-phase fallback references is defined by rule R8." .

###  Repetition policies

:ExecuteOnce rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :RepetitionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The phase executes a single time (default when no repetition policy is given)." .

:RetryOnFailure rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :RepetitionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "On failure the phase is re-attempted, up to hasRepetitionLimit attempts, before PhaseFailed becomes terminal and propagates (rule R10). Behavior-tree retry decorator." .

:RepeatUntilCondition rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :RepetitionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The phase executes repeatedly — each iteration closed by the inherited LOX completion condition — until the phase's hasRepetitionUntilCondition holds (e.g. repeat detect-mark-neutralize passes until the route-clear condition is true). Behavior-tree loop decorator." .

:MaintainContinuously rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :RepetitionPolicyCode ;
    rdfs:comment "A standing behavior: the phase remains active indefinitely, re-establishing its condition whenever violated (patrol, overwatch, communications relay), until preempted by order (e.g. SuspendPlanExecution/AbortPlanExecution, or lox:OtherOrderReceived). BDI maintenance-goal semantics. A standing phase should declare lox:OtherOrderReceived as its LOX completion condition." .

###  Goal commitment modes

:AchieveOnce rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :GoalCommitmentCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The goal is achieved when its achievement condition first becomes true; commitment then ends." .

:Maintain rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :GoalCommitmentCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The achievement condition must be kept true continuously; the system re-plans whenever it becomes false. Standing/persistent tasking." .

:AchieveThenMaintain rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :GoalCommitmentCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The goal is first achieved, then maintained until commitment is withdrawn by order." .

###  Condition predicates

:EntityAtLocation rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity is at the referenced location (object reference = location UUID; threshold value = tolerance in meters, optional)." .

:EntityWithinRange rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity is within range of the referenced entity or location (object reference = reference UUID; threshold value = range in meters)." .

:EntityHealthBelow rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity's health/operational status falls below the threshold value (0..1 fraction of full capability)." .

:ThreatDetectedInArea rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when a hostile or suspect entity has been detected within the subject area (object reference = optional entity-type filter)." .

:HazardOnRoute rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when a reported hazard (obstacle, IED, contamination) intersects the subject route. Use with isNegated true as the 'route is clear' guard or loop-termination condition." .

:CommsAvailable rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity has a usable communications link to the referenced entity (object reference; default: its command node)." .

:CommsDenied rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity has had no usable communications link for longer than the threshold duration. Gates degraded-mode contingency plans." .

:AreaCoverageAchieved rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the fraction of the subject area covered by search/survey reaches the threshold value (0..1). Provides the explore-until-covered termination criterion for search and reconnaissance goals." .

:EstimateConfidenceAbove rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the executing system's confidence in the referenced estimate or detection (object reference = track/estimate/observation UUID) reaches the threshold value (0..1). Supports belief-state gating such as switch-to-tracking on sufficient detection confidence, or repeat-measurement until a geolocation confidence ellipse converges." .

:PayloadCapacityAvailable rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity has at least the threshold value of payload capacity available (units per the platform's declared capacity model)." .

:TimeElapsedSince rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the threshold duration has elapsed since the referenced event (object reference = event UUID; default anchor: subject phase start)." .

:WeatherLimitExceeded rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when observed environmental conditions exceed the subject platform's declared operating limits (limits taken from the platform's initialization data, not carried in the condition)." .

:PayloadOnBoard rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the referenced payload, cargo, or person (object reference) is embarked on the subject platform. The embarkation-state predicate the CASEVAC walk found missing: 'casualty loaded' is a load state, for which EntityWithinRange is a false proxy." .

:RemainingEnduranceBelow rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject platform's remaining endurance (battery, fuel) falls below the threshold value (0..1 fraction of full endurance). Distinct from EntityHealthBelow, which conflates damage with depletion. Typical uses: return-to-base guard; bingo-energy loop termination (the STANAG 4586 Bingo Energy loop-limit analog)." .

:EntityImmobilized rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity is unable to move (trapped, mired, mechanically disabled), regardless of health state. The mobility-state predicate the MDARS walk found missing: 'trapped intruder' and 'stuck platform' are mobility facts, not health facts." .

:EntityInsideArea rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConditionPredicateCode ;
    rdfs:comment "True when the subject entity is inside the referenced area (object reference = TacticalArea/MapGraphic UUID). As a guard: keep-in enforcement (violation fails the phase, routing to a safe-hold fallback); with isNegated true: keep-out enforcement. Gives areas the enforced keep-in/keep-out binding that MAVLink geofences and STANAG 4586 restricted zones provide and base-standard symbology does not." .

###  Deviation types

:RouteChanged rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The system autonomously changed its route from the one planned or previously reported." .

:FallbackActivated rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "A phase failed and its on-failure fallback phase (or next-priority alternative) was activated." .

:PlanSwitched rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The system switched to a different transmitted plan for the same goal because context conditions changed (rule R14)." .

:GoalAbandoned rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "A goal's failure condition was met and the system withdrew commitment to it." .

:TaskReassigned rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "A task was autonomously reassigned to a different performing entity (e.g. within a swarm or team). NOTE: this reports a reassignment; constructs for commanding or constraining reassignment (capability declaration, allocation authority) are future work." .

:BehaviorAdjusted rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "The system autonomously adjusted an operating parameter of the current behavior (speed, altitude, standoff, sensor rate) without changing route, plan, or goal. The parameter-level deviation the DroneResponse and MDARS walks found unreportable with the v0.0.2 vocabulary." .

:ExceptionRaised rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "A plan-anticipated exception occurred (an exception trigger fired: intruder detected, casualty found, contact lost) and the system entered its scripted exception handling. Reported as a deviation so the operator sees anticipated-but-unscheduled transitions on the same channel as unscripted ones; hasActionTakenReference names the activated handling phase. (Decision recorded: modeled as a DeviationTypeCode value rather than a sibling alert report type, keeping one explainability channel.)" .

:LostLinkBehaviorActivated rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :DeviationTypeCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Communications loss exceeded hasLostLinkTimeout and the system executed its lost-link disposition (rule R18). Reported on restoration of communications, covering the interval: which behavior ran, from when to when, with rationale." .

###  Failsafe behaviors

:ReturnToBase rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :FailsafeBehaviorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Return autonomously to the launch point or designated base (MAVLink RTL analog)." .

:ReturnToRallyPoint rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :FailsafeBehaviorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Proceed autonomously to the nearest reachable location named by hasRallyPointReference (MAVLink rally-point analog)." .

:LoiterInPlace rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :FailsafeBehaviorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Hold at or near the current position (loiter, station-keep, or stop, per platform type) awaiting link restoration." .

:ContinueMission rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :FailsafeBehaviorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Continue executing the current plan autonomously without the command link (the STANAG 4586 continue-mission lost-link option). Commanders should pair this with HumanApprovalTrigger gates on any phase that must not proceed unsupervised: per rule R13 an approval gate cannot be satisfied while the link is down, so gated phases hold or take their timeout disposition." .

:TerminateMission rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :FailsafeBehaviorCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Cease mission activity and render the platform safe (land immediately / stop and safe payloads; STANAG 4586 flight-termination analog)." .

###  Additions to core code lists

:TASKFAILD rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskStatusCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Task failed: the task was attempted and did not achieve its purpose. Distinct from TASKABRT, in which execution was stopped by command or exception. Candidate erratum for the core TaskStatusCode list; carried in ASX until adopted." .

:TASKACPT rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskStatusCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Task accepted: the tasked entity commits to perform the task (FIPA agree; JAUS/4D-RCS tasking handshake). Reported per task via TaskStatus/TaskDispositionReportContent, closing the gap that acknowledgment codes are message-level only. Candidate erratum for the core TaskStatusCode list; carried in ASX until adopted." .

:TASKRJCT rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskStatusCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Task rejected: the tasked entity declines or cannot perform the task (FIPA refuse; the 4D/RCS 'cannot do because of condition xyz' reply). Use TaskDispositionReportContent to carry the rationale and the machine-readable infeasibility condition. Candidate erratum for the core TaskStatusCode list; carried in ASX until adopted." .

:TASKSUSP rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskStatusCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Task suspended: execution paused with state retained, pending resumption (rule R17; JAUS Pause Mission analog). The task-level counterpart of PhaseSuspended. Candidate erratum for the core TaskStatusCode list; carried in ASX until adopted." .

:ConfigureAutonomy rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskActionCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Configure autonomy: to set the autonomy level, permissions, or behavior parameters of an autonomous system." .

:SuspendPlanExecution rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskActionCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Suspend plan execution: to pause execution of the current plan while retaining state, pending resumption or amendment. With ResumePlanExecution, provides the mechanism for mid-mission re-tasking (suspend; transmit amended plan related by IMO 'is a modification of'; resume)." .

:ResumePlanExecution rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskActionCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Resume plan execution: to resume a suspended plan. Where a suspended plan has been superseded (rule R16), Resume targets the superseding plan; the superseded plan itself MUST NOT be resumed." .

:OverrideAction rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskActionCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Override action: operator override of a specific autonomous action or pending decision, without suspending the whole plan." .

:AbortPlanExecution rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskActionCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Abort plan execution: to terminate execution of the current plan; the system reverts to a safe default behavior." .

:AchieveGoal rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , c2sim:TaskActionCode ;
    rdfs:comment "Achieve goal: to accomplish the referenced Goal by means of the performing entity's own planning; the task conveys the end state, constraints, and ROE rather than a procedure. Goal-directed tasking." .

###  Hand-authored to match the OWL API serialization conventions of CSIM_ASX.rdf
